min_period: no check at nom_typ_1p20V_25C, nom_slow_1p08V_125C, nom_fast_1p32V_m40C (exception: no library the chip uses (the IHP SG13CMOS5L standard cell, SRAM and I/O .lib files) defines a minimum_period arc or a min_period attribute, so OpenSTA has no minimum-period check; the clock period is bounded by setup/hold and pulse width, which are gated)
clock_gating_setup: no check at nom_typ_1p20V_25C, nom_slow_1p08V_125C, nom_fast_1p32V_m40C (exception: the clock gates are the library's integrated clock-gating cells (sg13cmos5l_lgcp_1 and slgcp_1 are clock_gating_integrated_cell), whose enable is timed by their setup/hold arcs with every other register; OpenSTA infers clock-gating checks only for gating built from plain logic)
clock_gating_hold: no check at nom_typ_1p20V_25C, nom_slow_1p08V_125C, nom_fast_1p32V_m40C (exception: the clock gates are the library's integrated clock-gating cells (sg13cmos5l_lgcp_1 and slgcp_1 are clock_gating_integrated_cell), whose enable is timed by their setup/hold arcs with every other register; OpenSTA infers clock-gating checks only for gating built from plain logic)
